<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 388-393: Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis by equidistant coordinate-grid interpolation — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "E2/E6, E4, E5 and E7 are implemented as stated and mirrored by 11 Lean theorems; Pass 2 adds the numerical E1 check (min det D phi_t over the 9 x 8 grid and inside the form at 21 stages) that Lean states in 1-D, plus the coarse 9-anchor grid that realises Thompson's actual construction (few anchors, smooth grid, fold-free) beside the dense semilandmark spline. Remaining deduction: Fig. 389's drawn grid is still not digitised line by line, so phi is reconstructed from the silhouettes rather than read off the plate." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py L582–L600: phi fitted on silhouette configurations, not on Thompson's drawn grid lines <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7a7c0f5b6/thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L582-L600>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 388-393: Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis by equidistant coordinate-grid interpolation — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Quantitative morphometrics on the output are compared against the source's claim with explicit nulls and uncertainty: t* vs nominal with sweep SD; Procrustes, IoU, boundary RMSE, Pearson r and RMSE vs three controls; KS test of residual distributions (p <= 5.5e-6); 3! pairing permutation (nominal best, p = 1/6 floor); exact correspondence-shift null (95 shifts, p = 0.0104, z = -4.4). measure_morphoeval() exposes 11 measurements, 8 with reference values. Deductions: the permutation test has only 6 arrangements; no literature morphometrics of real intermediate taxa exist in the pinned data (part B)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
